,"H5359":"vengeance","H935":"come","H1576":"recompense","H1931":"he/she/it","H3467":"to save","H227":"then","H6491":"to open","H5869":"eye","H5787":"blind","H241":"ear","H2795":"deaf","H6605":"to open","H1801":"to leap","H354":"deer","H6455":"lame","H3956":"tongue","H483":"mute","H3588":"for","H1234":"to break up/open","H4325":"water","H5158":"river","H1961":"to be","H8273":"scorching","H98":"pool","H6774":"parched","H4002":"spring","H5116":"pasture","H8577":"jackal","H7258":"rest","H2682":"grass","H7070":"branch","H1573":"reed","H8033":"there","H4547":"highway","H1870":"conduct","H6944":"holiness","H7121":"call to","H3808":"not","H5674":"to pass","H2931":"unclean","H1980":"went","H191":"fool(ish)","H8582":"to go astray","H738":"lion","H6530":"violent","H2416":"alive","H1077":"not","H5927":"rise","H4672":"to find","H1350":"redeem","H6299":"to ransom","H7725":"return","H6726":"Zion","H7440":"cry","H8057":"joy","H5769":"enduring","H5921":"upon","H7218":"head","H8342":"rejoicing","H5381":"to overtake","H5127":"to flee","H3015":"sorrow","H585":"sighing"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Lily. Judea flourishes under Ezechias: but the Church does more so after the coming of Christ, to whom these expressions conduct us. (Calmet) — The Gentiles shall be converted and flourish, as this text shews. (Worthington)"],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Joy. The primitive Christians rejoiced in a good conscience, and in suffering for the truth."],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Knees. Ye prophets, comfort the people with these promises. (Calmet) — The apostles taught the Gentiles to do good. (Menochius)"],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Recompense. Christ will satisfy the justice of his Father. (Haydock) — He will redeem the world, and refute the false interpretations of the Bible. (Calmet) — He will bring the devil into subjection. (Menochius)"],["haydock",6,null,"haydock","Free. Our Saviour healed both soul and body, (Calmet) shewing by his works (John x.; Worthington) that he had fulfilled this prediction, Luke vii. 22., and Matthew xi. 5. — Waters. Baptism has sanctified the most wicked."],["haydock",7,null,"haydock","Dragons. Sea monsters, chap. xxxiv. 13. (Calmet) — All shall be in proper order, neither too dry nor too wet. (Haydock)"],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","Way, leading to Jerusalem. Idolaters, &c., shall not be there, chap. lii. 1. This was only verified (Calmet) in the Catholic Church, where, though some wicked may be found, the truth still prevails; and holiness can be obtained no where else. (Haydock) — This Church is unspotted, Ephesians v. 27. (Calmet) — Fools. The most simple may learn what is necessary for salvation, (Menochius) which will never be done by consulting Scripture alone. (Haydock)"],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","Lion. The devil’s power shall be repressed, so that none will be deluded except by their own fault. (Menochius)"],["haydock",10,null,"haydock","Sion. Before the defeat of Sennacherib, the roads were unsafe, chap. xxxviii. 8. (Calmet)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}